  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Metro Machine obligated $381M in FY2026 to date across 21 awards, with an average award size of $18.1M and obligations up 6.0% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $378M, while the Department of Transportation obligated $2.7M. Ship Building and Repairing accounted for $378M of obligations, and Other Support Activities for Water Transportation accounted for $2.7M. Metro Machine obligations climbed from $209M in FY21 to a peak of $524M in FY24, then moved to $359M in FY25 and $381M in FY26. Award volume remains concentrated: 21 awards produced the current-year total, and the average award size was $18.1M. The fiscal-year series shows year-to-year variability, with a notable increase between FY21 and FY24 and a partial pullback in FY25 before the current-year rise. Buyers and markets line up: Department of Defense and Ship Building and Repairing together represent the vast majority of current obligations, while Department of Transportation and water-transport support activities represent the remaining, much smaller shares.",
